LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF12", "label": "Study family SF12: A1 within-scheme re-test controlling early-third PPP selection", "score": 0.993, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-001 auto_related_family (repeat_order_unknown) FAM:SF12", "FAM:SF-APPA-001 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF12"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A1 within-scheme re-test controlling early-third PPP selection", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Within the same inferred scheme (and within early-PPP quintiles), adapters improve PPP more than wrong-way teams, and this carries to the next game.", "observed_result": ["[APPA-002] Within scheme gap: DROP +0.0830 (Welch p=0.0046), HELP +0.0539 (p=0.0493), SWITCH -0.0199 (p=0.6514). Quintile gaps -0.0440, -0.0231, +0.0138, +0.0133, +0.0966. Carryover gaps DROP +0.0039 (p=0.4244), HELP -0. [cut; read_family for the full text]", "[APPS-051] DROP: adapt +0.0041 vs wrong -0.0789, gap +0.0830, Welch p=0.0046, n=73/109. HELP: +0.0943 vs +0.0404, gap +0.0539, p=0.0493, n=96/115. SWITCH: +0.1200 vs +0.1399, gap -0.0199, p=0.6514, n=36/50. Pooled quinti [cut; read_family for the full text]"], "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)"}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF13", "label": "Study family SF13: Within-game did_adapt toward SHOULD counters improves PPP", "score": 0.851, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-001 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF13", "request matches RQC:RQC-002 (0.68); FAM:SF13 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-002"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Within-game did_adapt toward SHOULD counters improves PPP", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "Offenses that shift toward the counter play types for the inferred opponent scheme gain PPP later in the game.", "observed_result": ["[APPA-003] 531 rows with inferred scheme; 249 adapted (46.9%); adapters +0.0701 (n=239) vs non-adapters +0.0121 (n=269), advantage +0.0580 PPP; DROP +0.1001, SWITCH -0.0436, HELP +0.0450.", "[APPM-013] Adapter dPPP +0.0613 vs +0.0131; advantage +0.0482 PPP, p=0.0199. SWITCH subgroup reversed (-0.0160).", "[CHT-018] First run: adapters n=229 mean dPPP +0.0613 vs non-adapters; later 586 rows, 90.6% inferable, adapters +0.0701 vs non-adapters +0.0121, lift +0.058 (n=508). T1: no-signal baseline is highest dPPP so +0.05 lift  [cut; read_family for the full text]"]}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF27", "label": "Study family SF27: Linear team+opponent+play_type baseline vs simulation kernel", "score": 0.769, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-070 (0.66); FAM:SF27 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-070", "FAM:SF-PAP-098 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF27"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Linear team+opponent+play_type baseline vs simulation kernel", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "The Monte Carlo simulation kernel predicts margins better than a linear PPP~team+opponent+play_type model.", "observed_result": ["[CHT-004] SPOT_UP PPP 2.83 to 1.16 (fixed); linear margin R = +0.505; kernel Det. R = +0.466 (gap 0.001 vs linear additive R = +0.467); 5/5 perturbation tests.", "[PAP-097] linear Margin R=+0.505, win accuracy 64-68%; deterministic kernel R=+0.466 vs linear +0.467 (gap 0.001) after the multiplicative rewrite; earlier additive kernel compressed variance"], "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": ["[CHT-004] NOT_RECORDED", "[PAP-097] kernel R=+0.466 matches linear +0.467; does not beat the simple model"], "observed_sample_and_power": "[CHT-004] NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-098", "label": "Study family SF-PAP-098: Calibrated simulation vs Elo/net-rating/lineup+/- baselines", "score": 0.71, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-PAP-098 (0.71)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Calibrated simulation vs Elo/net-rating/lineup+/- baselines", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "The calibrated simulation beats simple team-level baselines on PPP MAE, win accuracy, log loss, and calibration error.", "observed_result": "VAL: CALIBRATION PPP MAE 0.1152 win 68.9% vs Elo 0.1154 / 69.4% and avg PPP 0.0928 / 67.9%; HOLDOUT: CALIBRATION PPP MAE 0.3369 win 54.8% logloss 0.778 vs Elo 0.3319 / 58.1% / 0.658 and lineup+/- win 64.5%", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "holdout win accuracy 54.8% vs lineup+/- 64.5% and Elo 58.1%; val-to-holdout collapse 68.9%->54.8%", "observed_sample_and_power": "val ~193 games; holdout 155 games", "auto_validation_status": "same_pipeline_validation; evidence: PAP-098: 'validation ~193 games mid-jan-feb; holdout 155 games late-feb through'"}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "score": 0.43, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-055 (0.68); FAM:SF-CHT-009 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-055"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.", "observed_result": "Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n>=30 for lineup cells cited", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-067", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-067: TOV_FORCE 3-ply adversarial surviving lift", "score": 0.423, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-032 (0.67); FAM:SF-APPA-067 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-032"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "TOV_FORCE 3-ply adversarial surviving lift", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Raw R1 TOV-force channel lifts survive opponent re-route or PT-shift (R2) and our follow-the-ball counter (R3).", "observed_result": "R1 lifts shrink ~50%+: ORL Banchero/Huerter +8.4 to net +3.7pp; DET Green/Anthony +7.0 to +3.5; PHI Harris/Vucevic +12.0 to +6.0; BOS Holiday/Council +6.1 to +2.8; PHX Booker/Wiggins +14.8 to +7.5; OKC Dort/Coffey +12.0  [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Net lift is model-implied, not observed in the games; R3 often additive surrogate at n<10.", "observed_sample_and_power": "4 games; 8 offense-defense sides", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "descriptive"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-010"}, {"rel": "auto_measures", "node": "VAR:turnovers"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-066", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-066: TOV_FORCE matchup decomposition on four playoff games", "score": 0.411, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-031 (0.65); FAM:SF-APPA-066 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-031"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "TOV_FORCE matchup decomposition on four playoff games", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "TOV_FORCE as a top-3 lever can be decomposed into defender x initiator x PT channels with positive matchup lift.", "observed_result": "Team-PT lifts are small (ORL vs DET PNR +1.2pp; POR vs SAS all PT lifts negative, e.g. PNR -4.1pp) while player-channel lifts are large on small n (Banchero on Huerter SPOT_UP +8.4pp, n_def=17 / n_off=54; Dort on Coffey  [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Player-channel n often 15-28 defensive possessions; primary_defender attribution includes helper steals; no holdout or game-outcome check.", "observed_sample_and_power": "4 games; cell n often 15-54"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:insufficient_exposure"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY"}]}], "n_results": 10}

